# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored; this template is committed.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# READ THIS BEFORE ADDING ANYTHING
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The game itself has NO runtime environment variables. It is a pile of static
# files with no backend (see docs/adr/0001-python-is-build-time-only.md).
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed VITE_ to the browser, and it does so by
# EMBEDDING THEM IN THE BUNDLE. A VITE_ variable is not a secret — anyone who
# opens the page can read it. Never put a credential behind a VITE_ prefix.
#
# Everything below is build-time only: used by scripts a developer runs, never
# shipped to a player.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# GitHub. Only needed if you script releases or use the gh CLI non-interactively.
# Prefer `gh auth login` over storing a token in a file.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Image generation for stylized art (character, storybook pages, backgrounds).
# Build-time only: art is generated once and committed under
# assets/images/generated/. Prompts are logged in prompts/.
# Planet and moon surfaces are NOT generated — those are real NASA imagery.
# NANO_BANANA_API_KEY=
